## ⚙️ Installation & Setup

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Kavinnnn-R/Blood-Donation-App.git
```

### 2️⃣ Open the Project

Open the project using **Android Studio**.

### 3️⃣ Configure the Server

Update the API/server URL in the Android application to point to the deployed backend.

```text
YOUR_SERVER_LINK
```

### 4️⃣ Build the Project

Allow Android Studio to download the required Gradle dependencies.

### 5️⃣ Run the Application

Connect an Android device or launch an Android Emulator.

Then click:

```text
Run ▶
```

---

## 🚀 How It Works

### 1. Register as a Donor

Users can provide their required information and register themselves as blood donors.

### 2. Request Blood

Users who require blood can submit a blood request.

### 3. Find Donors

The application retrieves available donor information from the backend server.

### 4. Match Donors

Donors can be identified based on the required blood group.

### 5. Connect

The donor and recipient can proceed with the necessary communication and donation process.

